%% Sleep spindle detection, reference-channel selection, and global/local classification
% This script preprocesses NREM thalamic EEG data by selecting the
% thalamic channels and filtering the signals between 7 and 15 Hz to
% isolate sleep spindle activity.
%
% Sleep spindles are detected independently for each thalamic channel,
% and the corresponding spindle peaks are identified from the filtered
% signals. A binary spindle-event matrix is then constructed across
% channels, and the mean event activity is calculated to characterize the
% temporal distribution of spindle activity.
%
% For each predefined group of eight thalamic channels, the channel with
% the largest number of detected spindle events is selected as the
% representative reference channel. The reference channel with the
% largest overall number of spindle events is then selected for further
% analysis.
%
% Spindle activity around the events of the main reference channel is
% extracted from the mean spindle-event signal, and the average spindle
% waveform is calculated. The mean signal amplitude during each spindle
% event is also calculated for each representative reference channel.
%
% Based on a predefined amplitude threshold of 0.76, spindle events are
% classified as global or local. The corresponding spindle events and
% real peak information are stored separately for global and local
% spindles for each representative reference channel.
%
% The resulting reference-channel information and global/local spindle
% classifications are saved in a MAT file. Generated figures are saved
% in both PNG and MATLAB FIG formats in the specified output directory.

